{"availability":"available","full":"showoffjp/usa-security-connect","name":"usa-security-connect","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-25T03:25:36Z","updated":"2026-10-08T06:10:50Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://usa-security-connect-xi.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://usa-security-connect.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.819Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.819Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.819Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:35:53.819Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The whole guard-force platform, with a demo company you can sign in to.","Scheduling, GPS time clock, post logs, payroll, invoicing and a client portal for a Florida security contractor, USA Security & Protection Group. It covers guard tours, time and attendance, incident reporting, supervision and billing, in one system:","All three talk to the same API, and the rules that decide \"late\", \"missed check-in\" or \"outside the geofence\" live in one shared module so no surface can disagree with another. One thing gets captured once: an officer's clock-in is the same record that produces their timesheet, the client's coverage report and the invoice line."],"features":["a web app for officers and the admin console,","a mobile app built from one codebase for Android and iPhone, and","a client portal where a site contact sees the service they are paying for.","Every screen, by area, with a picture of each from the demo company. Click a picture to see it full size. What it does, in detail has the rules behind each one.","Where everyone is right now, against where they are scheduled to be. Admin and supervisor."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/showoffjp/usa-security-connect/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b804c182503e2a88c0c0e68d2f1de0e3a66bd258842503beffdc0280c8a